## Harness Corrections

- Replaced the legacy teleport-only Grass positive path with explicit `MOVE_WALKING -> MOVE_FALLING -> MOVE_WALKING` cells.
- Final visual verification reuses the hashed initial temp-pass capture; it does not spawn QA actors into or reload the production map.
- Same-session Python active-map reload is prohibited because hidden `FPyReferenceCollector` references can trigger the fatal World leak guard.

## Research Basis

- [Unreal Engine World Position Offset Material Functions](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/world-position-offset-material-functions-in-unreal-engine): Chain a secondary foliage motion layer into the existing WPO.
- [Unreal Engine Pivot Painter Tool 1.0](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/unreal-engine/pivot-painter-tool-1.0?application_version=4.27): Keep every blade shape rigid and rotate around its packed root pivot.
- [GPU Gems 3 Chapter 16 - Vegetation Procedural Animation and Shading in Crysis](https://developer.nvidia.com/gpugems/gpugems3/part-iii-rendering/chapter-16-vegetation-procedural-animation-and-shading-crysis): Separate main directional bend from sine-family detail motion and vary phase per blade.
- [GPU Gems 3 Chapter 6 - GPU-Generated Procedural Wind Animations for Trees](https://developer.nvidia.com/gpugems/gpugems3/part-i-geometry/chapter-6-gpu-generated-procedural-wind-animations-trees): Use a bounded overshoot that decays as the restoring force settles.
